course: dictionary
lesson: 5027
title: Ingrown toenails
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An ingrown toenail is a toenail that grows into the skin instead of out of it. Ingrown is an adjective: it describes the nail or hair. «Toenails cut too short or curved can grow into the skin, which is called an ingrown toenail.» So the word tells you what has happened: the nail has grown in, not out.
explain: Ingrown can also describe a hair, as in «an ingrown hair». The edge of the nail or hair presses into the skin, which can hurt. «Cutting toenails straight across helps stop ingrown toenails, where the edge grows into the skin and can get sore and infected.»
explain: Look for the warning signs. «A sore, red, swollen toe beside the nail may be an ingrown toenail, so you tell a parent.» Telling an adult early is the smart move, because a doctor or podiatrist can help if it gets worse.
fact: Ingrown means grown into the skin instead of out of it.
fact: «An ingrown toenail» can hurt and may become infected.
fact: To help stop it, cut toenails straight across, not too short.
fact: Wear shoes that fit, so they do not squeeze your toes.
fact: A red, sore, swollen toe may need a doctor or podiatrist.
exercise: What does ingrown mean? | Grown very long and curly | *Grown into the skin instead of out of it | Grown out of the skin and away from it | Coloured red from the sun
exercise: How should you cut your toenails to help stop ingrown toenails? | Down into the sides of the toe | Only when they fall off | *Straight across, and not too short | Short and curved at the corners
exercise: A toe is red, sore and swollen beside the nail. What should you do? | Ignore it until it goes away | *Tell a parent, as it may be an ingrown toenail | Squeeze the swelling hard | Paint the nail to hide it
test: Which word describes a toenail that has grown into the skin? | Undergrown | *Ingrown | Outgrown | Overgrown
test: Why should your shoes fit well? | To make your toes look longer | To make your feet grow faster | To stop your socks from getting wet | *To help avoid ingrown toenails
exam: Which is the best next step for a red, sore, swollen toe beside the nail? | *Tell a parent, who can help you see a doctor or podiatrist | Cut the nail very short | Wrap the toe tightly and forget it | Wait and hope it stops
